WEBVTT

00:19:29.083 --> 00:19:32.018
AG: Alexi did leave
and started his own company,

00:19:32.042 --> 00:19:34.726
but the stress and self-doubt
didn't go away.

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:37.143
AR: Maybe I just can't be a founder CEO.

00:19:37.167 --> 00:19:38.893
I knew I was great as a number two.

00:19:38.917 --> 00:19:40.976
Maybe I just gotta make
my peace with that.

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:43.810
AG: He had hoped being his own boss
would solve the problem.

00:19:43.834 --> 00:19:45.601
AR: I did that for about three months

00:19:45.625 --> 00:19:47.434
and realized, nope, I am the problem.

00:19:47.458 --> 00:19:49.643
AG: So he decided
to try a professional coach.

00:19:49.667 --> 00:19:50.934
Her name was Heidi.

00:19:50.958 --> 00:19:53.518
AR: I learned that I am
a terrible overaccommodator.

00:19:53.542 --> 00:19:56.934
She would just keep pointing out
very gently, but very powerfully

00:19:56.958 --> 00:19:59.684
you didn't share with the person
what you actually thought

00:19:59.708 --> 00:20:02.476
or you didn't share with the person
how that bothered you.